{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Shall it be told to Him</b> — its meaning is: a person need not tell it to Him. If a man says in his heart, that He lacks something, it will not avail him. And Rav Hai Gaon, of blessed memory, said: for it means the sun is swallowed [eclipsed]."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {0 "The last phrase כי יבולע על השמש is obscure; rendered hyper-literally. The quotation attributed to Rav Hai Gaon does not clearly connect to the verse and may reflect a textual corruption or an abbreviated gloss."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:56.107427195Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}